<Project>
  <!--
    Conditionally suppress the Avalonia build-time telemetry target (Avalonia.BuildServices >= 11.3.x).

    What AvaloniaStats does:
      - Fires BeforeTargets="CoreCompile" on every build
      - Writes an anonymous telemetry record (hashed project name, TFM, Avalonia version,
        OS, IDE, CI environment, persistent machine GUID) to a local AppData directory
      - Spawns a background dotnet process (Avalonia.BuildServices.Collector.dll) that
        POSTs the records to https://av-build-tel-api-v1.avaloniaui.net/api/usage
      - Has no effect on the compiled output whatsoever

    Why it crashes in the Nix sandbox:
      Common.AppDataFolder calls Environment.GetFolderPath(LocalApplicationData,
      SpecialFolderOption.Create), which on macOS goes through NSFileManager and tries
      to create ~/Library/Application Support/AvaloniaUI/BuildServices. In the sandbox
      $HOME is /var/empty (mode 000), so mkdir fails with EPERM / UnauthorizedAccessException.
      This crash happens in a static initializer, *before* the AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1
      environment variable is checked, so the official opt-out cannot help here.

    Why Directory.Build.targets (not .props):
      Directory.Build.props is imported BEFORE NuGet package .targets, so any target
      defined there would be overridden by Avalonia.BuildServices.targets.
      Directory.Build.targets is imported AFTER NuGet .targets, so this empty definition
      wins and replaces the Avalonia one.

    The override is conditioned on NIX_BUILD_TOP, an environment variable that the Nix
    sandbox always sets (it points to the build's temp directory). It is never set during
    a normal developer build, so telemetry is left intact outside of Nix.

    To opt out of telemetry in non-Nix builds, set AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 in your
    environment; that is the official mechanism supported by Avalonia.
  -->
  <Target Name="AvaloniaStats" Condition="'$(NIX_BUILD_TOP)' != ''" />
</Project>
